9	+    # andesim (ROADMAP_LINUX_RUNTIME.md U9): on riscv64 with GGML_RVV, GCC's
10	+    # auto-vectorizer (specifically the SLP/straight-line pass, not the
11	+    # loop vectorizer -- confirmed by testing both `-fno-tree-vectorize`
12	+    # and a #pragma GCC push_options/optimize/pop_options wrapper, neither
13	+    # of which stopped it) lowers ordinary struct/array copies in generic
14	+    # dispatch/bookkeeping code (found: a struct-literal static init in
15	+    # ggml-cpu.cpp registering the CPU backend's device vtable, and an
16	+    # array copy in ggml-cpu.c's ggml_graph_plan) into 64-bit-element (e64)
17	+    # vector loads/stores. That is correct for any core meeting the RISC-V
18	+    # V extension's own spec-mandated ELEN>=64 floor, but the andesim
19	+    # hybrid-sim target (Andes ax45mpv) implements only Zve32f (ELEN=32)
20	+    # and traps on it.
21	+    #
22	+    # Rather than keep hunting individual auto-vectorized sites one at a
23	+    # time (whack-a-mole, with no way to be sure the next one has been
24	+    # found), this is inverted: DENY vector codegen by default for every
25	+    # generic/dispatch file (no computational reason for any of them to
26	+    # need a specific ELEN), and explicitly ALLOW-LIST only the files
27	+    # confirmed (by their own genuine, hand-written __riscv_v* intrinsic
28	+    # kernels -- not guessed) to need full v: vec.cpp and repack.cpp, and
29	+    # arch/riscv/{quants,repack}.cpp/.c (the whole point of the arch/riscv/
30	+    # split -- hand-written RVV quantization kernels). Everything else in
31	+    # GGML_CPU_SOURCES is generic op dispatch/graph bookkeeping with no own
32	+    # RVV code, so constraining it is free and closes off the whole bug
33	+    # class within those files, not just the two instances found here.
34	+    #
35	+    # This file-level mechanism does NOT cover every e64/vector-capability
36	+    # issue on this target -- an allow-listed file can still have individual
37	+    # functions that are wrong for ELEN=32 (or for this engine's narrower-
38	+    # than-spec vector-FPU LMUL ceiling; a distinct, RTL-only limit, see
39	+    # ROADMAP_LINUX_RUNTIME.md U9). Those got fixed AT the function, in the
40	+    # allow-listed file itself, not here: vec.cpp's ggml_vec_dot_f16/
41	+    # ggml_vec_dot_bf16 carry a per-function `__attribute__((target(...)))`
42	+    # override for the same auto-vectorization reason as above (their
